      "description": "Watch Kasimpasa vs Konyaspor highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 18, 2026. The Süper Lig returned to action on September 18, 2026, as Kasimpasa hosted Konyaspor in a match that promised tactical intrigue. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish dominance in what turned out to be a highly contested evening. A Cagey Opening and Disciplined Defenses The encounter began with high physical intensity, where space to create dangerous plays was scarce. Tactical discipline was the dominant note, but excessive defensive zeal soon resulted in bookings. Matei Cristian Ilie of Konyaspor received the first yellow card in the 24th minute, quickly followed by Claudio Winck for Kasimpasa . Before the interval, tension rose and Adil Demirbag also saw yellow, reflecting the difficulty both attacks faced in penetrating the respective defenses. Tactical Shifts and Physical Battles in the Second Half Upon the restart, the balanced scenario remained. Konyaspor continued to find it difficult to control the opposition's advances without resorting to fouls, with Marko Jevtovic and Rayyan Baniya being cautioned in short succession. Looking for solutions, the managers began to move their tactical pieces. Enis Bardhi replaced Jevtovic , while Kasimpasa responded by bringing on Haris Hajradinovic to refresh the midfield. Closing Stages and the Final Deadlock In the final twenty minutes, the rhythm of the game was constantly interrupted by strategic substitutions. Kasimpasa threw on Mostafa Mohamed and Jean-Luc Dompe to try and find a winning goal, but the visiting defense remained impenetrable. Near the end, the last cards were played with the introduction of Ebrima Colley and Adem Arous , but the final whistle at 90+4 confirmed a share of the points in a duel where defenses clearly outperformed the attacks."
